    Endothelial cells          35.98 CPM
    Eccrine gland duct         30.41 CPM
    Fibroblasts 1              23.81 CPM
    Immune cells 2             19.96 CPM
    Fibroblasts 2              18.65 CPM
    Keratinocytes 2            17.59 CPM
    Eccrine gland              16.86 CPM
    Hair follicle              16.13 CPM
    Keratinocytes 1            13.93 CPM
    Sebaceous gland            10.72 CPM
    Keratinocytes 3             9.93 CPM
    Immune cells 1              7.70 CPM
    Nevus                       7.57 CPM   <- melanocytic
    Tumor 2                     5.50 CPM   <- melanocytic
    Tumor 1                     2.14 CPM   <- melanocytic
  share of summed CPM in melanocytic compartments: 6.4%
  share of RASSF9 MOLECULES in melanocytic compartments: 17.1%
    (estimated as CPM x total_umi / 1e6, summed)

  The manuscript quotes 17.1%. Of the two definitions:
    summed CPM      6.4%  (sum of rates -- not a share of anything)
    molecule share  17.1%  (the quantity the wording implies)
  The molecule share MATCHES the published value. The manuscript
  sentence is correct as written and panel A can quote it.

